# Conversion makes every Mountain, whoever controls it, a Plains (CR 305.7, 613.1d): it taps for white, and a Taiga (a
# Mountain Forest) loses its Forest type too and taps for {W} alone, not {R} or {G}; each keeps its card type and the basic
# Mountain its supertype (the ruling: no supertype is added or removed); a Forest, which is no Mountain, is left alone.
